    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DxL9d5fu37W3m3zsfHHvEv)_\n\n**Before:** startup reports `[FAILED] sp-env (void-function exec-path-from-shell-copy-env)`. `sp-env.el` had a second, top-level `dolist` (added in ee21b24 for `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`) calling `exec-path-from-shell-copy-env` outside the `use-package` form. That form only loads the package in a GUI window system (`:when`), and under Elpaca its `:config` runs after activation, so the top-level call hit an unloaded package (always in a terminal Emacs). The list also contained a literal `...` left from an abbreviated edit, which would have been passed as a symbol.\n\n**After:**\n- `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` joins the single variable list inside `:config`; the stray top-level `dolist` is removed.\n- The daemon case (`(when (daemonp) ...)`, which also called the package outside `use-package`) becomes part of the `:if` condition, so the package loads and initialises there too.\n\n**Not tested:** nothing was run (no Emacs in the container). On fish, `exec-path-from-shell` is unchanged; if a startup warning about the shell appears, it is separate from this error.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01VmpaH7h5GRXDBJYjUQKtJQ)_",
